{"duration_api_ms":4531,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"31d99fe1-8cf4-4a89-8ee2-1bda84e34912","total_cost_usd":0.0009175,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1083,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":744},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1036,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1036},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1578,"outputTokens":1105,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1036,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0009175,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":744,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1036,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Yes, but the benefit is pooled, not reserved for mutual fund holders.\n\n**Mechanism:** Under IRC §852(b)(6), a RIC generally doesn't recognize gain when distributing appreciated securities in redemption of its shares. When ETF-class holders redeem in kind, the fund delivers low-basis securities, so embedded gains leave the portfolio unrealized. Since all classes share one portfolio, fewer realized gains mean smaller capital gains distributions, helping every class in proportion to its NAV.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The benefit depends on ETF-class redemption volume and which lots are delivered. Cash-based trading can still realize gains.\n- Mutual fund redemptions are typically cash, forcing sales that realize gains and partly offsetting the benefit.\n- Class-level expenses and in-kind basket costs must be allocated under the fund's multi-class plan (Rule 18f-3).\n- Benefits are shared pro rata, so MF holders get no dedicated advantage.","ttft_ms":3000,"type":"result","duration_ms":3944,"uuid":"5032665c-1673-4e36-947c-5d2ffd33cd2b","ttft_stream_ms":426,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":426,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
